---
import Layout from "../../../layouts/Layout.astro";

// The privacy policy for the Allday Bundles Shopify app
// (github.com/boccdotdev/allday-bundles-app). Its URL goes in the app's
// App Store listing, so keep the path stable.
const title = "Allday Bundles privacy policy · bocc(dot)dev";
const seoTitle = "Allday Bundles privacy policy";
const seoDescription =
	"What the Allday Bundles Shopify app does with information when a store installs it.";
const updated = "24 November 2026";
---

<Layout {title} {seoTitle} {seoDescription}>
	<main class="w-full p-8">
		<header
			class="border-b dark:border-grey-dark border-grey-mid pb-12 space-y-8"
		>
			<a href="/" class="font-mono text-sm">bocc(dot)dev</a>
			<h1 class="font-medium text-xl [text-wrap:balance]">
				Allday Bundles privacy policy
			</h1>
		</header>
		<article class="max-w-prose pt-12 pb-12 space-y-6 [text-wrap:pretty]">
			<p class="font-mono text-sm">Last updated: {updated}</p>
			<p>
				Allday Bundles is a Shopify app made by bocc(dot)dev (William
				Bocchinelli) for All Day. This policy explains what the app does
				with information when a store installs it.
			</p>

			<h2 class="font-medium text-lg pt-4">What the app processes</h2>
			<p>
				The app works out bundle savings for a store's carts. To do that,
				Shopify runs the app's discount function inside Shopify's own
				systems, with the contents of the cart: the products, their
				quantities and prices. That happens within Shopify. Cart contents
				are never sent to us and we keep no copy of them.
			</p>
			<p>
				The app's Admin page reads the store's bundle discount and the names
				of the products in it, and shows them to the staff member who opened
				it. Nothing it reads is stored.
			</p>

			<h2 class="font-medium text-lg pt-4">What the app stores</h2>
			<p>
				Nothing about customers. The only thing the app keeps is its bundle
				configuration, which is stored by Shopify in the store's own discount
				settings and contains products and savings, not people.
			</p>

			<h2 class="font-medium text-lg pt-4">Hosting</h2>
			<p>
				The app's Admin page and its Shopify webhooks are served by
				Cloudflare. Cloudflare may log technical details of each request
				(such as IP address and time) for security and reliability, under
				<a class="underline" href="https://www.cloudflare.com/privacypolicy/"
					>Cloudflare's own privacy policy</a
				>. Our logs record the type of request only, never its contents.
			</p>

			<h2 class="font-medium text-lg pt-4">Data requests</h2>
			<p>
				Shopify sends every app a notice when a customer asks to see or
				delete their data, or when a store uninstalls. Because the app holds
				no customer or shop data, there is nothing to send or delete, and we
				confirm that to Shopify.
			</p>

			<h2 class="font-medium text-lg pt-4">Contact</h2>
			<p>
				Questions about this policy:
				<a class="underline" href="mailto:contact@bocc.dev">contact@bocc.dev</a>.
			</p>
		</article>
	</main>
</Layout>
